<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90533" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτιόσσομαι</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		 Verb, only pres. and impf., and never
		in the form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσόσσομαι</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>look at</i> or <i>upon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδέ τιν᾽ ἀνθρώπων προτιόσσεο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				23.365
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of the mind,
				<i>forebode</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κραδίη προτιόσσετ᾽ ὄλεθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.389
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνατον προτιόσσετο θυμὸς ἀγήνωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.219
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.895
			</span></i>, al.; so, prob., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ σ᾽ εὖ
				γιγνώσκων προτιόσσομαι</span> from thorough knowledge of
			thee <i>I divine</i> my fate, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.356
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1372
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
